<title>JAPAN: Sakura Bank to change rules to allow share buyback.</title>
<headline>Sakura Bank to change rules to allow share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sakura Bank Ltd said on Tuesday it would change its company rules after a shareholders' meeting on July 27 to allow it to buy back up to 350 million of its own shares.  </p>
<p>The share repurchase is aimed at improving the company's return-on-equity ratio, a Sakura bank spokesman said.</p>
<p>He also said that the timing of the buy-back will be decided with consideration to the bank's business performance.</p>
</text>
